rep_region(r'''(1) `presentAt` gains `siteId?` additively''',
    r'''The three deeds' telling subjects register in PT's commit at ST-4 (§19b).''',
    r'''(1) `presentAt` gains `siteId?` additively and `SET_PRESENCE` at a site mints the placing `party_event` deed `party_reached_site` (ST's token for ENC-HL-04's event; `actAt` the site's anchor settlement; the deed's target the anchor `{kind:'settlement', id}` with the site as an optional `siteId` qualifier beside RN's `institution` / `factionId` / `stressorId` — a SUBJECT, never an actor ref), so `lastHeard`, the journey and the champions' visits read the site through its anchor; (2) THE PARTY CLEARING A DEN IS ONE ACT through PT's door: the DM's table record `RECORD_CLEARING(siteId)` (§6) mints `party_cleared_site`, and that door CALLS ST's one writer (`siteLedger.js :: applySiteEvent` — `cleared`, holder none, `causedBy` the deed; ST names PT's party door in the writer's closed caller list), so one act and one undo carry the deed and the site's event together (ST §7.2, S8, OD-ST-38); a DM who records only `SITE_HOLDER` still clears the den (no deed, no renown), and ST's writer is idempotent per (site, word, tick), so both acts in one week write one `cleared`; THE PARTY'S HAND ON A SITE MADE KNOWN is the deed `party_made_known_site`, recorded beside the DM's own `SITE_STATUS made_known` act (THE SITES' court-veil word; ST's caller list names no PT door for it), offered by PT2's batched suggestion when that act falls where the party is ("The party was at Thornwatch when its shrine became known — did they have a hand in it?"); each with its §3.3 row; (3) every PT card's WHERE may be `site` — `ENGAGEMENT_WHERE_KINDS`' `site` (fold §3.4), the site riding the card's `subject` dial and the proposals' anchor still a real settlement; `site` is a WHERE kind and a subject, NEVER an actor kind (a site has no mind, ST4); (4) no ST kind is a party kind and no PT kind targets a site — a den on the road is a fact of the world, never a call aimed at the party (ST16); (5) THE SITES' court veil (`keptSecret` · `made_known`) is never the host's reveal of the players' known places (§2.4). The three deeds' telling subjects register in PT's commit at ST-4 (§19b). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — `cure/D-ST-r2.md` route (ST-r2-19: "a party clearing a den is ONE act through PT's door: the `party_cleared_site` deed's door calls ST's one writer … one act, one undo for both"; HOST-r2-19: `revealed` becomes `made_known`) · RULINGS-ROUND2b ADDENDUM ST-r2-14 ("`site` is a WHERE kind (`ENGAGEMENT_WHERE_KINDS`) and a SUBJECT (the `subject` dial), NEVER an actor kind"): item (3) leaned on ST's withdrawn actor widening and item (1) put a site on an actor-ref target. REFINED (R2b-4): the clearing's table verb `RECORD_CLEARING` is named (0 everywhere, `cure/D-PT-r2b-probe/census-r2b-2.out`); whether the reveal should also be ONE act through PT's door is open for the chair (§20) — vetoable.]''', 'E13 §4 sites items')

