ins_after(r'''and `enemy_in_service` had two meanings · SEAMS-r1-12 · HOST-r1-5.]''',
    r'''

**THE ROAD ARM** [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — SEAMS-r2-14 · RULINGS-ROUND2b STOP-PR-2, RULED (a): "PT's `party_gate` WIDENED to a road WHERE (no new kind; CH's words unchanged); PT's row and PR's cite"; PR §8.2: "fired by a patrolled traversal of the DM's own move"; CH gives persons the same road arm (`person_at_the_gate` at `road{a, b}`, CH §18)]. With THE PATROLS lit (`patrolsEnabled`), when the DM's toggle moves the party from a known place to a town (`presentAt.fromIds` → `presentAt.settlementId`, from the nearer of `fromIds`; the same move the town's gate hears), the engagement pass walks the move's TRAVERSAL — the hops of the cheapest land route of the one travel physics (`distanceRead.js :: candidateRoutes(digest, from, to, 1)[0].path`; aspatially the relationship-graph path; a sea or teleport hop has no road half and meets no rider) — half by half (PR §2.2's ONE STRETCH KEY `road{a, b}`, its halves cut at the digest gate), and on each half calls PR's ONE encounter law `patrolEncounter` once per power whose riders stood on that road in the move's week (PR §8.1; presence from PR's placement for `presentAt.sinceTick`). The party's inputs to that law: `cover` from RN's `fameIn(worldState, {kind:'party'}, power, tick).scope`, read backwards as PR reads every traveller's (a famous party is known on sight); no home court, so `stance` reads strangers, doubled under a standing ban on the `party` key (PR's own ban factor); the draw's traveller key `party`. A NOTICED party meets the noticing court's posture through the SAME leaf — `gateDefault({ worldState, snapshot, actorRef: {kind:'party'}, settlementId: <the noticing court>, tick })`, the same order and reasons (ban · `polity_ban` · circumstance · renown · watch), the riders being that court's WATCH on the road — and a card is minted only where the default is not plain `admitted`. AT MOST ONE ROAD CARD PER MOVE (PR R33): the first noticed half along the traversal whose default is not plain `admitted`; riders of the move's ORIGIN and DESTINATION courts are never a road card (the destination is heard once, at its town's gate; the origin's posture was its own gate's); only the DM's last move of a session is walked, as only it is an arrival. The card's WHERE is `road{a, b}` on the half the riders stood on, its anchor the noticing court's town; its words the town's gate's (`refused` = turned back on the road · `admitted_under_watch` = let pass under the riders' eye) and the seal's `struck`; its default, as every party kind's, is that NOTHING HAS HAPPENED TO THE PARTY YET — the riders' orders are the court's course, the stop itself is played at the table (PT6), and a DM whose party took another road strikes the card. Riders never seek the party of their own accord (PR19): the road arm fires only on the DM's own move. TIER: `patrolsEnabled` (C16) with `partyEngagementsEnabled`; with PR dark there is no road card and the party's default holds. The traversal's route is an inference from the one travel physics, never the party's stated intention (PLAUSIBLE until PT-6's first measurement confirms `candidateRoutes` follows the path `hopWeeks` priced). **Felt:** "Ashford's riders have orders to turn the party back on the road to Tolle."''', 'E20 §9.2 road arm')

rep(r'''LIFTED: the DM's `PARDON_PARTY`; and a court's own pardon when its seat changes hands — read through PL's ONE seat-change read `seatChangedSince(worldState, settlementId, banTick)` (its tick form, PL §2) (both landed tails, `previousGovernments` and `seatTransitions`; RULINGS-ROUND1 ADDENDUM): the windowed edges that court minted lapse at the next weekly pass; a DM KILL/ASSIGN writes neither tail (and the DM's tick-less `CHANGE_RULING_POWER` counts only behind a later stamped row), so its card offers "lift this court's bans on the party" (PL's STOP-2 precedent, as CH §11).''',
    r'''LIFTED: the DM's `PARDON_PARTY`; and a court's own pardon when its seat changes hands — read through PL's ONE seat-change read in its EXACT KEY FORM, `seatChangedSince(worldState, settlementId, episode)` (PL §2), over both landed tails (`previousGovernments` and `seatTransitions`; RULINGS-ROUND1 ADDENDUM): when a `party_banned` verdict mints a windowed edge, the resolver records the banning court's `seatEpisodeKeyOf(worldState, courtId)` beside it on the party's sub-ledger (`banKeys: { settlementId, episode }`, ≤ 8 — an `ExclusionEdge` carries no mint tick and its shape is not changed); each week an edge whose court reads `seatChangedSince(…, episode).changed === true` lapses through the same lift and its key drops (a key also drops when its edge lapses, is pardoned or is lifted). The key form counts every row of both tails, the DM's tick-less `CHANGE_RULING_POWER` included; a DM KILL/ASSIGN writes neither tail, so its card offers "lift this court's bans on the party" (PL's STOP-2 precedent, as CH §11). [REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — R2b-1: the tick form read a ban tick no record held (`normalizeExclusionEdge` keeps `{ settlementId, kind, untilTick }` only), and it would have lifted a paragon's ban and the party's from the same court under two rules on a DM's `CHANGE_RULING_POWER`; CH's exact key form (CH §11, OD-CH-34) is now the one lift — vetoable.]''', 'E9b §9.3 ban lift by key')
